Some corrections:

Magicbane is great for Rogues because of the backstab damage. Engrave
Elbereth, toss daggers, and enjoy dealing damage like a nuclear bomb.

Stormbringer is an accident waiting to happen if you have any pets at
all. A self-teleporting lich is especially easy to untame, and an
especially nasty opponent. Also, I'm not sure you can pay off demons
while wielding Stormy.
http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Stormbringer

Chaotic heros can pay off named demons just fine. Choatic demons are a
totally different story.

All that info about alchemy isn't complete with a link to the wiki
because there is so much more to know:
http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Alchemy

The knight's move cockatrice corpse strategy is good, but not perfect.
Monsters can move and zap in the same turn, so you're not entirely
safe. Also, your corpse could miss. In any case, it's still a
reasonable strategy.
 http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Movement_tactics#Doors

Only wizards can safely enchant a cornuthaum to +7. Elven armor is
fair game for everybody.

You check if a worn amulet is reflection by bouncing a magic missile
off a wall, onto yourself.
 http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Amulet#Probabilities_and_use-testing


